1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He rounded Cape Horn twice during his period of service in sailing-ships
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Litteratur:''' Ålands Skeppsbefälhavareförening r.f. (utg.), ''Åländska sjökaptener genom tiderna - en biografi'', Mariehamn 2001.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Cap-Horniers des Iles Åland     ''' / 22.9.2025
2 CONT Alexandersson Mikael, mollyhawk, was born in Lemland, Åland, on 18.11.1906 and died in 1969.
2 CONT He made his first voyage in May 1923 in the barque PROMPT, Master Erik Nils Eriksson.
2 CONT Mikael Alexandersson obtained his Master Mariner's certificat in Mariehamn in 1932.
2 CONT He rounded Cape Horn twice during his period of service in sailing-ships, in the PROMPT.
2 CONT Mikael Andersson served as Chief Mate of the barque PROMPT for 15 months, as 2nd Mate of the s s CHARTERHAGE for 17 months and as Chief Mate of the s s THORNBURY for 27 months.
2 CONT He then served as Master of the s s THORNBURY, s s RIGEL, s s TAURI, m v   GERD, m v SVANEN and m v MAJ for a total of 6 years 7 months.
2 CONT He served in ships under the Swedish flag for 6 years, and then again in ships under the Finnish flag, as Master of the s s SANDÖ for 24 months and as Chief Mate of the s s  BORE  VII  for 14 months.
2 CONT He then served as Chief  Mate of the Swedish m v ROYAL PULP as from  22.11.1957 .   
2 CONT
