2 CONT
2 CONT '''Cap-Horniers des Iles Åland        ''' / Viitattu 21.9.2025
2 CONT Alexandersson John, Mollyhawk, was born in Lemland, Åland, on 21.9.1903 and died there in November 1976.
2 CONT He made his first voyage in 1923, in the 3-masted barque MONTROSA and subsequently sailed in the 3-masted barque PROMPT and the 4-masted barque ARCHIBALD RUSSELL.
2 CONT He obtained his Master Mariner's certificate in Mariehamn in 1931.
2 CONT John Alexandersson rounded Cape Horn four times : in the ARCHIBALD RUSSELL westwards in 1924 and eastwards in 1925 and 1933, and in the barquentine MOZART eastwards in 1935.
2 CONT John Alexandersson served as 2nd Mate in various steamers and as Chief Mate in the m v LYDIA, 3-masted schooner BALDER, m v VESTA, m v JOHANNES, barquentine MOZART, m v  TIIRA, and s s ULEA.
2 CONT He was Master of the m v DIONE, s s ULEA and m v HELENA.
2 CONT He left the sea in 1944 in order to become a farmer on his family estate in Flaka, Lemland.
2 CONT
2 CONT SUOMEN MERENKULKU192601.08.1926 NO 8
2 CONT https://digi.kansalliskirjasto.fi/aikakausi/binding/891067?term=John%20Alexandersson&page=19 Viitattu 21.9.2025
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Sanomia ja tervehdyksiä''
